  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVATION OF TIGER AND ITS HABITAT THROUGH UNIQUE LAW ENFORCEMENT AND LIVELIHOOD MODEL SUPPORT IN MANAS NATIONAL PARK</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Manas National Park (MNP) management through its Manas.Tigers smart protection programs identifies Illegal Natural.Resource Extractors.(INRE) and warns them about their repeat illegal activities.in the MNP. These INRE are then introduced to Aaranyak.livelihood program to support them with alternative.sustainable livelihood. So far 1400 households have been.covered under this program. This project plans to support.100 INRE, thus further securing the MNP and removing direct.threats to tigers, rhinoceros and Asian elephants. Project.objectives are, (1) Strengthen protection in MNP using Manas.Tigers protection model; (2) Reduce human disturbance in the.park by reducing dependence of 100 INRE using alternative.farm and non-farm livelihood options; and, (3) Monitor and.evaluate impacts of conservation interventions on the ground.using sets of indicators.</narrative>
  </description>
